💡 **SUGGESTION: `runAppend` helper is never used**

This helper duplicates the `wd3LoadFull(...).module.action({...})` boilerplate, but all three tests in this suite (`append: existing plain-text value…`, `append: ADF object…`, `append: unreadable existing field…`) inline their own `wd3LoadFull` + `action` calls instead of going through `runAppend`. Either use it in those tests (it would save ~8 lines each) or drop it — as-is it is dead code that may mislead the next reader into thinking the suite has a shared runner.

```javascript
function runAppend(opts, customParams) {
    var env = wd3LoadFull(opts);
    var params = {
        ticket: { key: 'PROJ-1', fields: { summary: 'Some story' } },
        initiator: 'user@x',
        customParams: customParams
    };
    var result = env.module.action(params);
    return { result: result, jiraUpdates: env.jiraUpdates };
}
```

